{"w":2400,"lines":[{"t":"Reading","x":0.82870978101624759,"c":1,"y":0.034273176595124077,"w":0.081407680511474623,"h":0.015580652459350142},{"w":0.81481480916341154,"t":"The Uffington White Horse is a unique, stylised representation of a horse consisting of","x":0.072016463628431213,"h":0.017667844522968212,"y":0.08127208486875348,"c":1},{"h":0.016003780005537038,"t":"a long, sleek back, thin disjointed legs, a streaming tail, and a bird-like beaked head.","c":1,"x":0.072016457349654672,"y":0.09883720915652261,"w":0.80041152954101558},{"y":0.11474168305265842,"w":0.8313570149739582,"c":1,"t":"The elegant creature almost melts into the landscape. The horse is situated 2.5 km from","h":0.017678314721205179,"x":0.071978656859239529},{"h":0.019664990185848885,"y":0.13035214294316921,"c":1,"x":0.071970929102539757,"w":0.80257232666015621,"t":"Uffington village on a steep slope close to the Late Bronze Age* (c. 7th century BCE)"},{"t":"hillfort of Uffington Castle and below the Ridgeway, a long-distance Neolithic** track.","x":0.072016477909191773,"w":0.79835388183593747,"y":0.14811542981727921,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"t":"The Uffington Horse is also surrounded by Bronze Age burial mounds. It is not far from","h":0.016195524146054074,"x":0.072016450123110948,"y":0.17432273271587206,"w":0.79218109130859371,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.069958836022268642,"t":"the Bronze Age cemetery of Lambourn Seven Barrows, which consists of more than 30","y":0.19186046495717735,"h":0.017503492402524912,"w":0.79835393269856769},{"c":1,"w":0.80246912638346357,"t":"well-preserved burial mounds. The carving has been placed in such a way as to make it","x":0.072016465515519601,"y":0.20930232543559812,"h":0.01598837238037687},{"c":1,"w":0.82316182454427089,"t":"extremely difficult to see from close quarters, and like many geoglyphs is best appreciated","y":0.22518842498202485,"x":0.071962775321649422,"h":0.019850062537670632},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"t":"from the air. Nevertheless, there are certain areas of the Vale of the White Horse, the valley","x":0.069958855882127108,"y":0.24263839808515397,"c":1,"w":0.83539093017578125},{"t":"containing and named after the enigmatic creature, from which an adequate impression","x":0.072016457352611765,"y":0.26017441844544931,"w":0.80041152954101569,"c":1,"h":0.017505204860116641},{"c":1,"w":0.79218109130859382,"x":0.072016450122531148,"h":0.015988372380376759,"t":"may be gained. Indeed on a clear day the carving can be seen from up to 30 km away.","y":0.27761627892363094},{"y":0.30232558124952313,"c":1,"w":0.81069956461588544,"t":"The earliest evidence of a horse at Uffington is from the 1070s CE when 'White Horse","x":0.072016472727678249,"h":0.015990084276322758},{"h":0.017441860778592888,"w":0.76131688435872402,"c":1,"y":0.31976744170135696,"t":"Hill' is mentioned in documents from the nearby Abbey of Abingdon, and the first","x":0.069958841668933763},{"c":1,"h":0.01896211648857915,"x":0.069958858742988919,"t":"reference to the horse itself is soon after, in 1190 CE. However, the carving is believed","w":0.81687240600585942,"y":0.33568904590508164},{"t":"to date back much further than that. Due to the similarity of the Uffington White Horse to","c":1,"x":0.069958839531752803,"y":0.35306242662837928,"w":0.83127573649088538,"h":0.016195524146054296},{"c":1,"x":0.069958840449851803,"h":0.017464116549183006,"t":"the stylised depictions of horses on 1st century BCE coins, it had been thought that the","y":0.37063953472387901,"w":0.82510289510091139},{"x":0.074074073882111222,"y":0.38808139521095453,"w":0.36213991800944006,"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"creature must also date to that period.","c":1},{"t":"However, in 1995 Optically Stimulated Luminescence (OSL) testing was carried out by","h":0.017441860778592999,"w":0.81687240600585931,"c":1,"y":0.41279069751543251,"x":0.072016471789983147},{"y":0.42861669757445042,"h":0.018839649654249113,"c":1,"w":0.81901250203450526,"x":0.069910793409627178,"t":"the Oxford Archaeological Unit on soil from two of the lower layers of the horse's body,"},{"t":"and from another cut near the base. The result was a date for the horse's construction","w":0.81289825439453123,"h":0.018946376930838893,"y":0.44433215546362259,"x":0.071938817950481848,"c":1},{"y":0.46366279108486619,"h":0.01896382838452515,"t":"somewhere between 1400 and 600 BCE - in other words, it had a Late Bronze Age or","w":0.81481480916341154,"c":1,"x":0.072016463699629774},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"Early Iron Age origin.","x":0.074074072848567735,"c":1,"y":0.4811046510088649,"w":0.20164609273274739},{"w":0.81069956461588544,"c":1,"x":0.072016472750855764,"h":0.015988372380376759,"t":"The latter end of this date range would tie the carving of the horse in with occupation of the","y":0.50581395334210821},{"h":0.017441860778592888,"t":"nearby Uffington hillfort, indicating that it may represent a tribal emblem marking the land of","y":0.5232558137943476,"w":0.81687240600585942,"c":1,"x":0.072016471800945212},{"x":0.072016449184238329,"t":"the inhabitants of the hillfort. Alternatively, the carving may have been carried out during a","w":0.7983539326985678,"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.54063604264873122,"c":1},{"t":"Bronze or Iron Age ritual. Some researchers see the horse as representing the Celtic*** horse","h":0.018883358042147469,"x":0.074029088854923944,"y":0.55652722937222132,"w":0.83548522949218751,"c":1},{"x":0.072016461754570382,"t":"goddess Epona, who was worshipped as a protector of horses, and for her associations with","w":0.8271604919433595,"c":1,"y":0.57412790736591357,"h":0.018922740635237245},{"h":0.017441860778592888,"y":0.59156976728289179,"w":0.83127573649088538,"t":"fertility. However, the cult of Epona was not imported from Gaul (France) until around the first","c":1,"x":0.069958839467712253},{"w":0.82716049194335939,"c":1,"x":0.072016461753774283,"h":0.016048292108362783,"t":"century CE. This date is at least six centuries after the Uffington Horse was probably carved.","y":0.6089517080330995},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.62632508816736776,"c":1,"w":0.80246912638346368,"x":0.072016465512236422,"t":"Nevertheless, the horse had great ritual and economic significance during the Bronze and"},{"y":0.64244186069560505,"t":"Iron Ages, as attested by its depictions on jewellery and other metal objects. It is possible that","h":0.017452132154269218,"w":0.83539093017578114,"c":1,"x":0.072016466763961284},{"x":0.072016471850036692,"c":1,"t":"the carving represents a goddess in native mythology, such as Rhiannon, described in later","y":0.65988372076986046,"w":0.81687240600585942,"h":0.017441860778592888},{"y":0.67726737341707,"w":0.72016459147135425,"c":1,"x":0.07407408275039444,"t":"Welsh mythology as a beautiful woman dressed in gold and riding a white horse.","h":0.016046580212416783},{"y":0.70053003549898085,"c":1,"w":0.84156377156575513,"t":"The fact that geoglyphs can disappear easily, along with their associated rituals and meaning,","h":0.017493220465202852,"x":0.072016468211809487},{"y":0.71937573600136839,"c":1,"x":0.069958859567164494,"t":"indicates that they were never intended to be anything more than temporary gestures. But","h":0.016195524146054185,"w":0.81069956461588544},{"x":0.071961773243102226,"c":1,"w":0.83138656616210938,"t":"this does not lessen their importance. These giant carvings are a fascinating glimpse into the","y":0.73496779656597955,"h":0.01873105883738746},{"t":"minds of their creators and how they viewed the landscape in which they lived.","x":0.074074076493047675,"c":1,"y":0.75290697659788819,"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.70576131184895841},{"h":0.010306242638398078,"c":1,"w":0.69341562906901044,"t":"*Bronze Age: a period (in Britain c. 2,500 BCE - 800 BCE) that is characterised by the development of bronze tools","x":0.084362144210350695,"y":0.84010600703950522},{"w":0.79629628499348959,"h":0.011778563015312105,"y":0.85453474702061938,"c":1,"x":0.080246919128503014,"t":"**Neolithic: a period (in Britain c. 4,000 BCE - c. 2,500 BCE) that is significant for the spread of agricultural practices, and the use of"},{"y":0.87063953479172529,"x":0.090534978500039692,"t":"stone tools","w":0.067901236216227207,"c":1,"h":0.008720930389296444},{"x":0.074074081183366614,"w":0.50823043823242187,"t":"***Celtic: an ancient people who migrated from Europe to Britain before the Romans","c":1,"h":0.010306242638398189,"y":0.88515901032417355},{"w":0.026748971939086874,"x":0.88477366219918097,"y":0.90552325553798929,"h":0.014534883982160851,"c":1,"t":"39"}],"h":3396}